===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gem-pro|ine-pro|inh=1}}
{{suffix|de|Eichhorn|-chen}}, diminutive of {{m|de|Eichhorn}}, {{glossary|folk etymology}} based on {{m|de|Eiche}} and {{m|de|Horn}}, but actually from {{inh|de|gmh|eichurne}}, from {{der|de|goh|eihhorno}}, from {{der|de|gmw-pro|*aikwernō}}.

Cognate with {{cog|ang|acol||frightened}},<ref>{{R:Duden}}</ref><ref>{{R:DWDS}}</ref> also {{cog|nl|eekhoorn}}, {{m|nl|eekhoorntje}}, {{cog|fy|iikhoarntsje}}, {{cog|enm|aquerne}}, {{cog|da|egern}}, {{cog|nb|ekorn}}, {{cog|sv|ekorre}}, {{cog|is|íkorni}}.

